7e8a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542220 #edb/ref 1074 "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}]+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{aligned}],\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542244 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542244 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ec118fb-8e61-556c-8854-cbf857a4c88b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542244 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186229664 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542252 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186542272 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542252 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "488b9d3b-a97f-5cfc-9ee9-56aee87c9e33" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542252 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186372703 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186542267 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "8454